# ---------------------------------------------------------------- derived art
#
# Everything below is produced by a script in tools/ and is never edited by
# hand, so the source it is cut from is what belongs in git. See the pictures
# section of CLAUDE.md. A fresh clone has to run both scripts before it can
# build: the components import these files by name.

# The photographs. tools/photos.mjs cuts each one from the camera master
# sitting beside it in the same year folder, to twice the largest its slot is
# ever painted. The masters are tracked; these are not.
src/assets/[0-9][0-9][0-9][0-9]/*.webp

# The hero loop and its poster frame, both rendered by tools/hero-loop.mjs
# from src/scene/synthwave.js.
src/assets/hero-loop.webm
src/assets/hero-still.webp

# src/assets/wave.webp is deliberately NOT in this list. It has no script and
# no master in the tree -- it arrived as a lossless WebP that was compressed
# once, by hand, and the original is only in the first commit. That makes it a
# source file, not an artifact.
